.TH SDL_HINT_LOGGING 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_LOGGING \- A variable controlling the default SDL log levels.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_LOGGING \(dqSDL_LOGGING\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This variable is a comma separated set of category=level tokens that define the default logging levels for SDL applications\[char46]
.PP
The category can be a numeric category, one of \(dqapp\(dq, \(dqerror\(dq, \(dqassert\(dq, \(dqsystem\(dq, \(dqaudio\(dq, \(dqvideo\(dq, \(dqrender\(dq, \(dqinput\(dq, \(dqtest\(dq, or
.BR *
for any unspecified category\[char46]
.PP
The level can be a numeric level, one of \(dqverbose\(dq, \(dqdebug\(dq, \(dqinfo\(dq, \(dqwarn\(dq, \(dqerror\(dq, \(dqcritical\(dq, or \(dqquiet\(dq to disable that category\[char46]
.PP
You can omit the category if you want to set the logging level for all categories\[char46]
.PP
If this hint isn\(aqt set, the default log levels are equivalent to:
.PP
.BR app=info,assert=warn,test=verbose,*=error
.PP
If the
.BR DEBUG_INVOCATION
environment variable is set to \(dq1\(dq, the default log levels are equivalent to:
.PP
.BR assert=warn,test=verbose,*=debug
.PP
This hint can be set anytime\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

